=== 6. what is NOT the mechanism (tests of the additive-pentagon story) ===
   [ok] additive pentagon c1 = t + t^-1 and pentagram c2 = t^2 + t^-2:  c1 c2 = c1 + c2 and c1 + c2 = J - I  (so c^2 + c - 1 = 0 off constants)
   [ok] R_e c1 = c2 R_e (e swaps pentagon and pentagram), R_o commutes with c1
   [ok] but 2K does NOT commute with c1
   [ok] the golden plane W is NOT invariant under the additive pentagon c1
   golden eigenvector f: |proj on V1|^2 = 15*sqrt(5) + 35 = 68.541020,  |proj on V2|^2 = 15*sqrt(5) + 35 = 68.541020  (both non-zero: f lies in neither D5-isotypic plane)
   [ok] golden eigenvector lies in neither V1 nor V2
   [ok] 2K_5 is not normal (A A^T != A^T A) although its spectrum is real
   singular values of 2K_5: 0, sqrt(2), sqrt(2), 2, 2  (no golden ratio: phi is in the eigenvalues, not the singular values)
   automorphisms of the branch digraph: 1 (identity only); anti-automorphisms (reversals): 0
   Latimer-MacDuffee sanity: of 104 integer 2x2 matrices with charpoly x^2+x-1 (|a11| <= 12, |a12| <= 200), 104 are GL2(Z)-conjugate to the
   pentagon/A_4 block [[0,1],[1,-1]] (conjugator [v, Mv] with |v| <= 60).  So 'conjugate to the pentagon block' says nothing beyond the characteristic polynomial.

=== 7. over Q: when does the folded pentagon close? ===
   push-forward of point masses at rational points (valid mod every N prime to 6):
     delta_0 + delta_{-1}       ->  (delta_0 + delta_{-1}) + (delta_{1/2} + delta_{-1/2})        [always]
     delta_{1/2} + delta_{-1/2} ->  2 delta_{-1/4} + delta_{1/4} + delta_{5/4}
     delta_{-1/4}               ->  delta_{-1/8} + delta_{1/8}
   [ok] the configuration {-1/4; +-1/2; 0,-1} closes ({1/4,5/4} = {-1,0} and {+-1/8} = {+-1/2}) only for N = 5 among N < 2000 prime to 6

